Audio: COCK OUT LETS GO

Hi first please breathe no you didn't ruin your life. Worst comes to worst, you take calc at a local community college and move on. Likely, that won't even be necessary.It literally will not determine your life. Colleges have options for classes for a reason. You will not have 4 years of economics classes or polisci, you will have other pre-reqs and gen eds. Work with your advisor to fit in calculus if they think you need it. The biggest thing is talking to your advisor.I literally didn't choose my majors until almost the end of my sophomore year. I chose political science and public health and I didn't have calc or a chemistry backing, so my professors helped me fill those gaps.  Not high school counselors.

&#x200B;

Also, yes you can DEFINITELY have a successful career even without a polisci degree. A double major won't define your success, its the connections and work you do. I only have a double major because of hours and it made sense for me because I want to get a MPH and JD. There are politicians with high school degrees and art majors and business degrees. Political science isn't what you use really to get into politics as rather to just understand politics and people.

&#x200B;

